  <div style="margin-top: 30px; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">
    <p>Dependent Variable: Immigrants make country a worse (0) or a better (10) place. Factor: 1= years 2002-2006; 2= 2008-2010. ESS Database (round 1-5).</p>
    <p>As in Table 1 the ANOVA test shows the economic crisis indeed played a role in increasing prejudice in these countries. The F value of between-groups sum of squares of the means is significant. Instead, in the total sample made of the 25 European countries included in the ESS database (see Table 2), the between-groups difference is not significant. Therefore, the economic crisis indeed increased prejudice in the most affected countries but there is no evidence of this for all 25 European countries.</p>
